1
00:00:01,871 --> 00:00:05,005
["Flower Ring" by Shino Shimoji
and Aya Suzaki plays]

2
00:01:32,875 --> 00:01:34,398
- Spring passed us by,

3
00:01:34,529 --> 00:01:37,488
and the sun began shining down
stronger each day.

4
00:01:37,619 --> 00:01:39,969
The vegetables look brighter
and more colorful

5
00:01:40,100 --> 00:01:42,319
after they've been
sunbathing for a while.

6
00:01:43,755 --> 00:01:45,888
[Hiraku sighs]

7
00:01:46,018 --> 00:01:47,150
Hey, girls.

8
00:01:47,281 --> 00:01:49,109
- Huh?
- [Hiraku] It's break time.

9
00:01:49,239 --> 00:01:50,327
Let's have lunch.

10
00:01:50,458 --> 00:01:51,546
- Yay!

11
00:01:51,676 --> 00:01:53,461
- Okay.
- Let's go.

12
00:01:53,591 --> 00:01:55,071
- [Sena] I'll get
everything ready.

13
00:01:55,202 --> 00:01:56,333
- I'm starving.

14
00:01:56,464 --> 00:01:57,769
- Thanks.

15
00:01:58,466 --> 00:01:59,684
Hmm.

16
00:02:01,164 --> 00:02:03,775
This one might grow
too tall like this.

17
00:02:07,083 --> 00:02:09,520
I feel like I'm much more
knowledgeable about this stuff

18
00:02:09,651 --> 00:02:11,696
than when I first
started farming.

19
00:02:11,827 --> 00:02:13,785
Let's see about
the other plants.

20
00:02:13,916 --> 00:02:15,439
- [Lu] Darling.
- Oh.

21
00:02:15,570 --> 00:02:16,614
Huh?

22
00:02:16,745 --> 00:02:17,876
Lu?

23
00:02:18,007 --> 00:02:20,662
- Come on, it's time
for a break.

24
00:02:20,792 --> 00:02:22,838
[gentle music]

25
00:02:22,968 --> 00:02:23,969
- [Beast Girl]
Well, did you remember

26
00:02:24,100 --> 00:02:25,449
to bring the silverware?

27
00:02:25,580 --> 00:02:28,322
- You know, Hiraku,
you need to take breaks too.

28
00:02:28,452 --> 00:02:29,801
- Huh?

29
00:02:29,932 --> 00:02:33,109
When I look at the crops,
I can't help myself.

30
00:02:33,240 --> 00:02:35,677
- Mm.
- Hmm?

31
00:02:35,807 --> 00:02:38,984
[Lu giggles]

32
00:02:39,115 --> 00:02:40,464
Magic really is great.

33
00:02:40,595 --> 00:02:43,119
- I've told you,
this is just basic stuff.

34
00:02:44,033 --> 00:02:44,947
[Hiraku sighs]

35
00:02:45,077 --> 00:02:46,557
- I feel refreshed.

36
00:02:46,688 --> 00:02:49,343
- If you work too hard,
your body could collapse.

37
00:02:49,473 --> 00:02:51,475
- Don't worry, I'll be fine.

38
00:02:51,606 --> 00:02:52,998
But more importantly,

39
00:02:53,129 --> 00:02:55,087
is it okay for you
to be walking around?

40
00:02:55,218 --> 00:02:57,046
- Yeah, I'm okay now.

41
00:02:57,177 --> 00:03:00,005
In fact, I've heard it's
good to get exercise.

42
00:03:00,136 --> 00:03:01,746
- [Hiraku] Is that right?

43
00:03:01,877 --> 00:03:04,619
- [Lu] Everyone's been
teaching me all kinds of stuff.

44
00:03:04,749 --> 00:03:06,229
- [Sena] I heard from
the girls in the village
that it's important...

45
00:03:06,360 --> 00:03:07,752
- [Lea] Reproduction
and prosperity.

46
00:03:07,883 --> 00:03:09,319
- [Sena] to exercise
to keep your body strong.

47
00:03:09,450 --> 00:03:11,539
- After speaking with a few
of the ogre maid girls

48
00:03:11,669 --> 00:03:14,455
I found out that they've
actually given birth themselves.

49
00:03:14,585 --> 00:03:15,934
- That's reassuring.

50
00:03:16,065 --> 00:03:17,284
- Yeah.

51
00:03:17,414 --> 00:03:21,418
- I don't know anything
about that stuff.

52
00:03:21,549 --> 00:03:25,074
It's strange to think that she
has a child inside her belly.

53
00:03:25,205 --> 00:03:28,512
I wonder what that
must feel like for her.

54
00:03:28,643 --> 00:03:30,688
- So what is it actually like?

55
00:03:30,819 --> 00:03:33,691
Now that you've gotten so big,
it's got to feel heavy.

56
00:03:33,822 --> 00:03:35,171
- It does.

57
00:03:35,302 --> 00:03:37,173
It feels the same as
two heads of cabbage.

58
00:03:37,304 --> 00:03:40,176
- I'm guessing that means,

59
00:03:40,307 --> 00:03:42,134
you must feel pretty heavy then.

60
00:03:42,265 --> 00:03:44,615
- How lovely,
I'm so very jealous.

61
00:03:44,746 --> 00:03:48,053
- I wonder if it'll be a boy
or maybe a little girl.

62
00:03:48,184 --> 00:03:50,186
- Is there any way
to know that now?

63
00:03:50,317 --> 00:03:52,928
- Is there anything we can do
to make you more comfortable?

64
00:03:53,058 --> 00:03:55,757
- Please let us know how best
we can help you, Lu.

65
00:03:55,887 --> 00:03:57,237
- Thank you.

66
00:03:57,367 --> 00:03:59,804
You've all been so helpful
so I'm okay.

67
00:03:59,935 --> 00:04:01,850
My appetite is back now too.

68
00:04:01,980 --> 00:04:03,765
The only thing bothering me is,

69
00:04:03,895 --> 00:04:05,114
- [All] Hmm?

70
00:04:05,245 --> 00:04:07,551
- that I can't drink
any alcohol.

71
00:04:07,682 --> 00:04:11,207
- [All] Oh.

72
00:04:15,037 --> 00:04:15,864
- [Granmaria] Mayor.

73
00:04:15,994 --> 00:04:17,126
- Oh.

74
00:04:17,257 --> 00:04:18,606
- Forgive our insolence,

75
00:04:18,736 --> 00:04:20,695
but we have come to make
a request of you today.

76
00:04:20,825 --> 00:04:23,524
- [Hiraku] Okay. What is it?

77
00:04:23,654 --> 00:04:25,177
- We are here to ask that Tia

78
00:04:25,308 --> 00:04:27,615
and everyone else's
resolution not go to waste.

79
00:04:27,745 --> 00:04:29,617
- They've become so dejected.

80
00:04:29,747 --> 00:04:31,575
[Latismoon and Hakuren groaning]
- We beg of you.

81
00:04:31,706 --> 00:04:33,316
So please,

82
00:04:33,447 --> 00:04:35,536
sell off all the rest of
the alcohol in the village.

83
00:04:35,666 --> 00:04:36,928
- Huh?

84
00:04:37,059 --> 00:04:39,844
I see you're all giving up
alcohol for Lu.

85
00:04:39,975 --> 00:04:41,629
- That's right, however...

86
00:04:41,759 --> 00:04:44,284
- When we think about not
being able to drink we just...

87
00:04:44,414 --> 00:04:45,763
- [Hakuren] When we're
eating we think,

88
00:04:45,894 --> 00:04:47,243
"Man, some alcohol
would go great with this."

89
00:04:47,374 --> 00:04:48,549
It feels like...

90
00:04:48,679 --> 00:04:50,202
[all whining]

91
00:04:50,333 --> 00:04:52,466
Just like that.
- [Hiraku] It's that bad?

92
00:04:52,596 --> 00:04:54,250
- I believe at this point,

93
00:04:54,381 --> 00:04:56,252
the only option is to
remove the source.

94
00:04:56,383 --> 00:04:57,775
- Calm down.

95
00:04:57,906 --> 00:04:59,473
I'm happy that you're
all doing this,

96
00:04:59,603 --> 00:05:02,519
but I think you'll regret it
if we sell all the alcohol,

97
00:05:02,650 --> 00:05:05,479
and alcohol isn't something
we can make quickly.

98
00:05:05,609 --> 00:05:08,046
Just think of it
this way instead,

99
00:05:08,177 --> 00:05:11,746
the taste of alcohol changes
the longer you let it age.

100
00:05:11,876 --> 00:05:14,879
If you hold out now,
it'll taste better later.

101
00:05:15,010 --> 00:05:17,969
Let's all tough it out while
looking forward to that.

102
00:05:21,538 --> 00:05:24,498
- Forgive us, Mayor,
but we'd like for you to tell us

103
00:05:24,628 --> 00:05:26,717
if we've done something
to wrong the village.

104
00:05:26,848 --> 00:05:28,850
- Why? What happened?

105
00:05:28,980 --> 00:05:31,809
- Even though everyone used
to love drinking alcohol,

106
00:05:31,940 --> 00:05:33,811
none of them will drink
a single drop now.

107
00:05:33,942 --> 00:05:35,073
- [Hiraku] Oh.

108
00:05:35,204 --> 00:05:37,685
- Really? So that's all it was.

109
00:05:37,815 --> 00:05:39,774
So it's not like they
stopped enjoying

110
00:05:39,904 --> 00:05:42,516
the alcohol we produce.
- Of course not.

111
00:05:42,646 --> 00:05:45,519
I'm sorry, we should have
told you right away.

112
00:05:45,649 --> 00:05:46,868
- I was beginning to think

113
00:05:46,998 --> 00:05:48,913
that we should slow down
production.

114
00:05:49,044 --> 00:05:51,612
Now I think the opposite.
- You're right.

115
00:05:51,742 --> 00:05:53,918
They'll drink more to
make up for lost time.

116
00:05:54,049 --> 00:05:57,705
- [Donovan] Great, we'll do our
best to live up to expectations.

117
00:06:00,751 --> 00:06:04,102
[gentle serene music]

118
00:06:05,713 --> 00:06:06,670
[Daga sighs]

119
00:06:06,801 --> 00:06:10,370
[water splashing]

120
00:06:10,500 --> 00:06:13,285
[wind blowing]

121
00:06:17,768 --> 00:06:19,509
- You feeling okay?

122
00:06:19,640 --> 00:06:21,163
- Yeah, I'm fine.

123
00:06:21,293 --> 00:06:23,034
I'm not in here because of that.

124
00:06:23,165 --> 00:06:25,689
It's just the sun is
really strong today.

125
00:06:25,820 --> 00:06:27,778
- [Hiraku] It's almost time,
isn't it?

126
00:06:27,909 --> 00:06:29,737
- It looks that way.

127
00:06:29,867 --> 00:06:31,260
If I get any bigger than this

128
00:06:31,391 --> 00:06:33,131
I won't be able to move at all.

129
00:06:33,262 --> 00:06:35,003
- Where'd you get that?

130
00:06:35,133 --> 00:06:38,572
- Tia and the angels came
to visit me and brought it.

131
00:06:38,702 --> 00:06:40,878
They said they found it blooming
on a far away mountain

132
00:06:41,009 --> 00:06:43,359
where there was still snow.
- [Hiraku] It's pretty.

133
00:06:43,490 --> 00:06:45,405
It kind of makes
the room feel cooler.

134
00:06:45,535 --> 00:06:46,884
- Believe it or not

135
00:06:47,015 --> 00:06:48,669
that flower is actually
releasing cold air.

136
00:06:48,799 --> 00:06:50,888
- Hmm, pardon?

137
00:06:51,019 --> 00:06:52,324
- [Both] Hmm?

138
00:06:52,455 --> 00:06:54,326
- This is secret
mountain elf medicine.

139
00:06:54,457 --> 00:06:57,460
It brings about good health
and vigor, for you.

140
00:06:57,591 --> 00:07:01,290
- [Lu] Oh, this is really
valuable, isn't it?

141
00:07:01,421 --> 00:07:03,423
- I'd rather it be used
at the right time

142
00:07:03,553 --> 00:07:05,773
than have it just sit around
in storage forever.

143
00:07:05,903 --> 00:07:07,252
- [Hiraku] It sounds like
she's talking

144
00:07:07,383 --> 00:07:08,863
about a rare game item.

145
00:07:08,993 --> 00:07:10,430
- Hi, Lu.

146
00:07:10,560 --> 00:07:12,606
This gem is meant to help
with magic recovery.

147
00:07:12,736 --> 00:07:14,738
I found it in my father's
treasure room.

148
00:07:14,869 --> 00:07:16,218
- Oh, wow.

149
00:07:16,348 --> 00:07:19,395
- After much work,
it's finally perfected.

150
00:07:19,526 --> 00:07:20,831
I made pudding.

151
00:07:20,962 --> 00:07:22,354
- Mm.

152
00:07:22,485 --> 00:07:23,486
- Here.

153
00:07:23,617 --> 00:07:24,922
It's a good luck charm wreath.

154
00:07:25,053 --> 00:07:26,489
[Lu giggling]

155
00:07:26,620 --> 00:07:29,057
- Are you okay? Do you want
me to peel you apples?

156
00:07:29,187 --> 00:07:30,319
- Good afternoon.

157
00:07:30,450 --> 00:07:31,929
You must be hungry.

158
00:07:32,060 --> 00:07:34,279
I made tomato and tofu miso soup

159
00:07:34,410 --> 00:07:35,542
- Tomato?

160
00:07:35,672 --> 00:07:36,804
- [Lu] Mm.

161
00:07:36,934 --> 00:07:37,935
- [Hiraku]
It's surprisingly good

162
00:07:38,066 --> 00:07:39,633
- [Flora] Isn't it?

163
00:07:44,507 --> 00:07:46,248
- All lizard men are
born from eggs.

164
00:07:46,378 --> 00:07:50,121
Therefore, I have absolutely
no idea how best to help out.

165
00:07:50,252 --> 00:07:51,949
But at the very least,

166
00:07:52,080 --> 00:07:55,475
I offer my blood to drink
so that you'll grow stronger.

167
00:07:55,605 --> 00:07:57,825
- [Lu] I don't think that my
teeth can make it through that.

168
00:07:57,955 --> 00:07:59,043
- [Daga] Aw...

169
00:07:59,174 --> 00:08:02,351
[lively upbeat music]

170
00:08:06,834 --> 00:08:08,226
- [Hiraku] I'm really happy.

171
00:08:08,357 --> 00:08:09,576
- Yeah.

172
00:08:09,706 --> 00:08:11,273
[both chuckling]

173
00:08:13,623 --> 00:08:14,885
- What's this?

174
00:08:15,016 --> 00:08:16,626
A mallet?

175
00:08:16,757 --> 00:08:18,454
- It came from Donovan.

176
00:08:18,585 --> 00:08:21,065
He said to trust him that it
would come in handy one day.

177
00:08:21,196 --> 00:08:22,240
- Hmm.

178
00:08:22,371 --> 00:08:23,851
Come in handy?

179
00:08:23,981 --> 00:08:25,896
Do you need a mallet
for childbirth?

180
00:08:26,027 --> 00:08:27,289
Huh?

181
00:08:27,419 --> 00:08:28,638
What's wrong?

182
00:08:28,769 --> 00:08:30,379
- Mm.

183
00:08:33,730 --> 00:08:36,254
My belly feels kind of...

184
00:08:36,385 --> 00:08:39,214
- Does that mean?
- Mm.

185
00:08:39,344 --> 00:08:41,259
I think that it's time.

186
00:08:42,783 --> 00:08:44,480
- Bring the towels here.

187
00:08:44,611 --> 00:08:46,656
We need to boil more water.

188
00:08:46,787 --> 00:08:48,092
Here's some more wood.

189
00:08:48,223 --> 00:08:50,268
[maids panting]
[footsteps echoing]

190
00:08:50,399 --> 00:08:53,097
[Lu groaning]

191
00:08:56,840 --> 00:09:00,061
[gentle serene music]

192
00:09:03,238 --> 00:09:04,544
- [Hiraku] When the time came,

193
00:09:04,674 --> 00:09:08,896
I found myself in
a panic for a bit,

194
00:09:09,026 --> 00:09:12,290
but now there's nothing left
that I can do to help out.

195
00:09:12,421 --> 00:09:14,684
[gentle serene music]

196
00:09:18,470 --> 00:09:20,821
[wind blowing]

197
00:09:24,346 --> 00:09:27,567
[footsteps echoing]

198
00:09:31,614 --> 00:09:34,835
[gentle serene music]

199
00:09:39,361 --> 00:09:41,189
The two moons.

200
00:09:41,319 --> 00:09:42,582
On my first night here,

201
00:09:42,712 --> 00:09:45,410
I watched them from
this very place.

202
00:09:47,674 --> 00:09:49,197
Back then, I was alone.

203
00:09:49,327 --> 00:09:53,331
I wanted to live somewhere by
myself away from everyone,

204
00:09:54,506 --> 00:09:56,596
but now everyone's here.

205
00:09:56,726 --> 00:09:59,207
That's why I am sure that...

206
00:10:00,948 --> 00:10:04,081
After that time passed
like a blur until morning.

207
00:10:04,212 --> 00:10:06,083
Well, it's more
accurate to say

208
00:10:06,214 --> 00:10:09,347
that I don't have any memories
of what happened after that.

209
00:10:13,134 --> 00:10:15,179
- Mm.

210
00:10:15,310 --> 00:10:16,485
- Everything went really great.

211
00:10:16,616 --> 00:10:18,922
- Mother and baby
are doing very well.

212
00:10:22,926 --> 00:10:24,711
[Hiraku gasps]

213
00:10:29,716 --> 00:10:31,282
- Come hold him.

214
00:10:33,328 --> 00:10:34,764
- Can I really?

215
00:10:36,548 --> 00:10:38,594
I, um.

216
00:10:38,725 --> 00:10:39,856
- Be careful.

217
00:10:39,987 --> 00:10:41,510
- He was just born,
watch his neck.

218
00:10:41,641 --> 00:10:43,817
- Make sure to support it
with your arm.

219
00:10:43,947 --> 00:10:45,166
- Okay.

220
00:10:46,254 --> 00:10:48,648
[gentle spirited music]

221
00:10:50,040 --> 00:10:54,001
He's warm and he's
heavier than I expected

222
00:10:54,131 --> 00:10:57,004
even though he's so small.

223
00:10:57,134 --> 00:10:59,006
Oh, he moved.

224
00:10:59,136 --> 00:11:00,616
- Of course he moves, you silly.

225
00:11:00,747 --> 00:11:02,705
He was moving when he
was still in my belly.

226
00:11:02,836 --> 00:11:05,621
- Oh, I see.

227
00:11:06,970 --> 00:11:08,798
Ah, he smiled.

228
00:11:08,929 --> 00:11:10,582
That was a smile, right?

229
00:11:10,713 --> 00:11:13,760
- He must be really happy
that his dad's holding him.

230
00:11:13,890 --> 00:11:15,326
- Oh.

231
00:11:17,981 --> 00:11:20,810
Oh, that's right.

232
00:11:20,941 --> 00:11:23,683
I've really become a father.

233
00:11:24,553 --> 00:11:26,250
Back in my original world,

234
00:11:26,381 --> 00:11:28,513
I was suffering from an illness.

235
00:11:28,644 --> 00:11:32,343
I hope he never has to
go through that.

236
00:11:32,474 --> 00:11:34,737
Grow up to be big and strong.

237
00:11:37,566 --> 00:11:40,090
- He's not going to just
grow up strong.

238
00:11:40,221 --> 00:11:43,528
We'll raise him to be
strong together.

239
00:11:46,793 --> 00:11:48,533
- That he will.

240
00:11:51,014 --> 00:11:52,059
[baby crying]

241
00:11:52,189 --> 00:11:53,495
What's wrong?
What should I do?

242
00:11:53,625 --> 00:11:55,584
- [Sena] Please calm down.

243
00:11:55,715 --> 00:11:57,151
- [Lea] Everyone, just relax.

244
00:11:57,281 --> 00:11:59,370
- [Lu] It's okay.
[Hiraku chuckling]

245
00:12:00,328 --> 00:12:03,679
[bright upbeat music]

246
00:12:07,030 --> 00:12:08,292
- [Hiraku] All done.

247
00:12:08,423 --> 00:12:10,991
It's been a week since
Lu gave birth.

248
00:12:11,121 --> 00:12:13,515
My son's name is Alfred.

249
00:12:13,645 --> 00:12:15,822
That was Lu's idea.

250
00:12:15,952 --> 00:12:19,434
I guess his race is technically
maybe half vampire,

251
00:12:19,564 --> 00:12:21,915
but right now he still looks
like a normal human.

252
00:12:22,045 --> 00:12:23,873
[everyone gushing]

253
00:12:27,572 --> 00:12:29,966
This is where I started
living by myself.

254
00:12:33,578 --> 00:12:36,190
A lot more people live here now.

255
00:12:37,539 --> 00:12:39,280
There are more
buildings now too.

256
00:12:39,410 --> 00:12:42,022
Everything kept growing.

257
00:12:42,152 --> 00:12:45,765
Now it's a village where I live
together with everyone.

258
00:12:45,895 --> 00:12:47,288
Then one day,

259
00:12:48,985 --> 00:12:50,682
I became mayor,

260
00:12:51,814 --> 00:12:56,601
and now I finally
become a father.

261
00:12:56,732 --> 00:12:58,821
Speaking of which,
I need to do something

262
00:12:58,952 --> 00:13:01,302
to thank the villagers
for their kindness.

263
00:13:01,432 --> 00:13:03,391
They've all been working
so hard up until now

264
00:13:03,521 --> 00:13:05,480
to help build up the village.

265
00:13:06,002 --> 00:13:08,700
Hmm.

266
00:13:08,831 --> 00:13:11,747
- Oh, what did you want
to talk to us about?

267
00:13:11,878 --> 00:13:13,357
- The thing is,

268
00:13:13,488 --> 00:13:15,969
I've been thinking about a
new system I want to set up.

269
00:13:16,099 --> 00:13:17,753
- [Tia] A system?

270
00:13:17,884 --> 00:13:19,059
- That's right.

271
00:13:19,189 --> 00:13:21,322
Like this.

272
00:13:21,452 --> 00:13:22,584
It's a reward medal.

273
00:13:22,714 --> 00:13:23,715
- A medal?

274
00:13:23,846 --> 00:13:26,196
- I see, what is it for?

275
00:13:26,327 --> 00:13:28,677
- As thanks for helping
to build the village.

276
00:13:28,808 --> 00:13:31,201
I want to give these medals
out to everyone.

277
00:13:31,332 --> 00:13:35,075
- So then how exactly are we
supposed to use these?

278
00:13:35,205 --> 00:13:37,207
- You can trade them
for goods you want

279
00:13:37,338 --> 00:13:39,122
or use them to get other
things you're after.

280
00:13:39,253 --> 00:13:42,778
- So you mean these act like
a money exchange, right?

281
00:13:42,909 --> 00:13:44,127
- Yeah.

282
00:13:44,258 --> 00:13:45,955
I figured that one day
this village

283
00:13:46,086 --> 00:13:47,783
will need its own currency.

284
00:13:47,914 --> 00:13:51,004
Right now we have a lot
of stuff in the village.

285
00:13:51,134 --> 00:13:53,833
Crops, hunted game meat,
and traded goods.

286
00:13:54,877 --> 00:13:56,183
As mayor of the village,

287
00:13:56,313 --> 00:13:58,272
I've been taking charge
of all these things

288
00:13:58,402 --> 00:14:00,970
and then distributing
them to everyone myself.

289
00:14:01,101 --> 00:14:03,146
Whenever someone
wants something,

290
00:14:03,277 --> 00:14:05,540
they come and ask me about it.

291
00:14:05,670 --> 00:14:07,759
But with the increasing
population here,

292
00:14:07,890 --> 00:14:09,761
handling all of
these transactions

293
00:14:09,892 --> 00:14:11,459
has become impossible.

294
00:14:11,589 --> 00:14:12,982
- I see.

295
00:14:13,113 --> 00:14:14,897
If we're going to handle
transactions on our own

296
00:14:15,028 --> 00:14:16,594
then we need currency.

297
00:14:16,725 --> 00:14:18,074
- [Hiraku] That's right.

298
00:14:18,205 --> 00:14:20,120
- Can't we just all trade
goods with each other?

299
00:14:20,250 --> 00:14:22,209
- Think about it this way.

300
00:14:22,339 --> 00:14:24,385
How many strawberries
for an apple?

301
00:14:24,515 --> 00:14:27,127
- Well, I'd say three
strawberries.

302
00:14:27,257 --> 00:14:28,563
- I'd say they're one to one

303
00:14:28,693 --> 00:14:30,608
since I much prefer
strawberries.

304
00:14:30,739 --> 00:14:31,914
- See?

305
00:14:32,045 --> 00:14:33,307
Everyone has their
own idea of value.

306
00:14:33,437 --> 00:14:35,439
That's why I want to
use currency

307
00:14:35,570 --> 00:14:37,224
for all our
transactions.

308
00:14:37,354 --> 00:14:39,574
- So that's what money
is meant to be used for.

309
00:14:39,704 --> 00:14:42,011
- [Hakuren] How many barrels
of gold is an apple worth?

310
00:14:42,142 --> 00:14:44,622
- [Latismoon] I almost never
use money so I'm not sure.

311
00:14:44,753 --> 00:14:46,233
- You count it in barrels?

312
00:14:46,363 --> 00:14:48,322
- I expect nothing less
from the dragons.

313
00:14:48,452 --> 00:14:50,715
- Anyways, it would
cause turmoil

314
00:14:50,846 --> 00:14:53,153
if I switched us
to currency right away.

315
00:14:53,283 --> 00:14:55,851
So for now, I'm going to
give these out as rewards.

316
00:14:55,982 --> 00:14:57,244
That's the plan.

317
00:14:57,374 --> 00:14:59,115
- I see then.
Well, in that case,

318
00:14:59,246 --> 00:15:01,074
let's try them out
for a while.

319
00:15:01,204 --> 00:15:02,771
- Sounds great.

320
00:15:02,902 --> 00:15:05,905
For now, let's just think of
these as convenient vouchers.

321
00:15:06,818 --> 00:15:08,342
And so to get things going,

322
00:15:08,472 --> 00:15:11,258
I started by giving all the
villagers three medals each.

323
00:15:11,388 --> 00:15:12,824
I couldn't give out medals

324
00:15:12,955 --> 00:15:14,739
to all of Kuro and
Zabuton's families,

325
00:15:14,870 --> 00:15:16,219
so I gave them 30 each.

326
00:15:16,350 --> 00:15:19,179
On top of that, I have to
make them all by hand

327
00:15:19,309 --> 00:15:21,398
in a way that they can't be
counterfeited.

328
00:15:21,529 --> 00:15:23,009
That limits how many I can make.

329
00:15:23,139 --> 00:15:24,836
Everyone reacted differently.

330
00:15:24,967 --> 00:15:27,535
- [Donovan] Give me wine.
[dwarves laughing]

331
00:15:27,665 --> 00:15:30,103
- [Hiraku] Some people traded
them for wine right away.

332
00:15:30,233 --> 00:15:33,454
Some people traded them
for furniture and the like.

333
00:15:33,584 --> 00:15:35,412
Some traded them for weapons

334
00:15:35,543 --> 00:15:37,675
that Dryme had brought us
as gifts.

335
00:15:37,806 --> 00:15:42,637
And some people just decorated
their rooms with them.

336
00:15:42,767 --> 00:15:44,944
I'd prefer if they didn't
just hold onto them

337
00:15:45,074 --> 00:15:46,336
without spending any.

338
00:15:46,467 --> 00:15:48,730
That's how I started
introducing the medals

339
00:15:48,860 --> 00:15:53,169
that were the precursors
for currency, but let's see.

340
00:15:53,300 --> 00:15:54,910
Oh, I've got it.

341
00:15:55,041 --> 00:15:57,304
It resulted in orders
for custom made furniture

342
00:15:57,434 --> 00:16:00,220
and toys to become
incredibly popular.

343
00:16:00,350 --> 00:16:03,353
If anything, I feel like
I'm doing more work now.

344
00:16:04,789 --> 00:16:06,313
Just wait a little while for me.

345
00:16:06,443 --> 00:16:08,184
I wanted to use these
as a guide

346
00:16:08,315 --> 00:16:10,665
for how much things are worth,
but it's hard to determine

347
00:16:10,795 --> 00:16:13,798
how much a single medal
should be worth.

348
00:16:14,886 --> 00:16:15,800
- [Beast Girl Kid] Mayor!

349
00:16:15,931 --> 00:16:16,845
- [Both] Oh?

350
00:16:16,976 --> 00:16:18,107
- I want you to give me...

351
00:16:18,238 --> 00:16:21,589
a baby just like that one!

352
00:16:21,719 --> 00:16:23,591
- Is that an option?
- [Hiraku] It's not!

353
00:16:23,721 --> 00:16:25,549
- What if I give you three?

354
00:16:25,680 --> 00:16:28,204
- That's not really the issue
we're having here.

355
00:16:28,335 --> 00:16:29,814
[Lu chuckles]

356
00:16:29,945 --> 00:16:32,034
[children laughing]
- [Hiraku] In the end,

357
00:16:32,165 --> 00:16:36,952
we settled on them renting out
the mayor for a day instead.

358
00:16:37,083 --> 00:16:38,998
And a little while after that,

359
00:16:39,128 --> 00:16:42,566
[villagers chattering]

360
00:16:50,052 --> 00:16:51,706
it was finally time
for the big feast

361
00:16:51,836 --> 00:16:54,665
to celebrate the birth
of my son.

362
00:16:55,927 --> 00:16:58,060
- [All] Cheers!

363
00:16:58,191 --> 00:17:01,542
[cheerful festive music]

364
00:17:03,500 --> 00:17:04,806
- I feel kind of bad.

365
00:17:04,936 --> 00:17:06,764
I kept them waiting a while.

366
00:17:06,895 --> 00:17:09,637
- Yeah, we couldn't have a feast
right after you gave birth.

367
00:17:09,767 --> 00:17:13,119
Well, they all seem to be
enjoying themselves now.

368
00:17:13,249 --> 00:17:16,513
I am a little worried that they
might drink too much though.

369
00:17:16,644 --> 00:17:20,604
- Hi there!
It's your Aunt Flora!

370
00:17:20,735 --> 00:17:22,737
- By the way, is that?

371
00:17:22,867 --> 00:17:24,260
- It is.

372
00:17:24,391 --> 00:17:27,046
Donovan told me to bring it
here with me today.

373
00:17:30,049 --> 00:17:31,789
- Sorry we took so long.

374
00:17:34,401 --> 00:17:36,098
- [Hiraku] What's this?

375
00:17:36,229 --> 00:17:37,795
- It's a special
new kind of wine

376
00:17:37,926 --> 00:17:39,884
that we made just for you
to have tonight.

377
00:17:40,015 --> 00:17:41,930
This is our way of
celebrating with you

378
00:17:42,061 --> 00:17:43,845
so make sure you do it right.

379
00:17:43,975 --> 00:17:46,500
It's time to whack it!
- Oh, you mean this?

380
00:17:46,630 --> 00:17:49,503
- I see, so that's
what it's for.

381
00:17:52,201 --> 00:17:54,856
- [Both] And smash!

382
00:17:54,986 --> 00:17:56,858
[everyone cheering]

383
00:17:56,988 --> 00:18:00,514
[cheerful festive music]

384
00:18:02,124 --> 00:18:03,125
[Lu chuckling]

385
00:18:03,256 --> 00:18:04,692
- That felt really good to hit.

386
00:18:04,822 --> 00:18:06,433
- Yeah, it sure did.

387
00:18:06,563 --> 00:18:09,479
I never thought I'd be
cracking open a barrel of wine

388
00:18:09,610 --> 00:18:11,307
in celebration in this world.

389
00:18:11,438 --> 00:18:13,309
I guess doing something big
like this

390
00:18:13,440 --> 00:18:15,006
always makes things more fun.

391
00:18:15,137 --> 00:18:17,748
Hey guys, drink up!

392
00:18:17,879 --> 00:18:20,490
[cheerful festive music]

393
00:18:25,060 --> 00:18:26,540
- Man, this booze is great.

394
00:18:26,670 --> 00:18:28,803
The food is great,
congratulations.

395
00:18:28,933 --> 00:18:31,284
Now time for my
secret technique.

396
00:18:35,157 --> 00:18:36,854
- Is she okay there?

397
00:18:36,985 --> 00:18:40,119
- Well, what do you
think of the wine?

398
00:18:40,249 --> 00:18:41,337
- Donovan?

399
00:18:41,468 --> 00:18:43,644
- Well, the thing is...
- Hmm?

400
00:18:44,384 --> 00:18:45,950
Ah, I get it.

401
00:18:46,081 --> 00:18:47,604
- I'm sorry.

402
00:18:47,735 --> 00:18:49,867
I've been told I shouldn't
drink while breastfeeding.

403
00:18:49,998 --> 00:18:51,391
- [Donovan] I see.

404
00:18:51,521 --> 00:18:53,219
You can't drink as long as
he's still a baby.

405
00:18:53,349 --> 00:18:54,611
I get it.

406
00:18:54,742 --> 00:18:56,396
- Right now, I'll let
them drink for me.

407
00:18:56,526 --> 00:18:59,877
I'll enjoy the wine by watching
all their smiling faces.

408
00:19:01,357 --> 00:19:02,793
- I've got an idea.

409
00:19:02,924 --> 00:19:04,491
How about before
everyone drinks it all?

410
00:19:04,621 --> 00:19:06,275
We bottle it so we can age it.

411
00:19:06,406 --> 00:19:08,103
- That sounds great.

412
00:19:08,234 --> 00:19:11,062
We can hold it until Alfred
is old enough to drink it.

413
00:19:11,193 --> 00:19:12,325
- Great idea.

414
00:19:12,455 --> 00:19:13,413
- All right.

415
00:19:13,543 --> 00:19:15,371
I'll keep it safe and age it

416
00:19:15,502 --> 00:19:17,373
so it's the best wine ever.

417
00:19:17,504 --> 00:19:19,027
Get started on this right away.

418
00:19:19,158 --> 00:19:20,594
If we drag our feet,
they'll drink it all.

419
00:19:20,724 --> 00:19:22,117
- I want more.

420
00:19:22,248 --> 00:19:24,119
- The day I drink with my son...

421
00:19:24,250 --> 00:19:26,252
I can't hardly wait for that.

422
00:19:26,382 --> 00:19:27,992
- That day will be soon.

423
00:19:28,123 --> 00:19:31,387
As long as you're enjoying life
every day like this.

424
00:19:32,388 --> 00:19:33,824
- [Flora] Look.
- [Both] Hmm?

425
00:19:33,955 --> 00:19:35,783
- Alfred, the sweet
little dumpling,

426
00:19:35,913 --> 00:19:38,394
loves his Aunt Flora so much.

427
00:19:38,525 --> 00:19:41,005
I think he wants to be my baby.

428
00:19:41,136 --> 00:19:42,442
- Stop right there

429
00:19:42,572 --> 00:19:45,009
- [Beezel] About the
Great Tree Village.

430
00:19:45,140 --> 00:19:46,359
- [Grattz] What is it this time?

431
00:19:46,489 --> 00:19:48,665
- [Beezel] The mayor
and vampire had a child.

432
00:19:48,796 --> 00:19:50,319
It was a healthy baby boy.

433
00:19:50,450 --> 00:19:51,799
- [Grattz] Oh, that's lovely.

434
00:19:51,929 --> 00:19:53,757
- Based on the information
we've heard so far,

435
00:19:53,888 --> 00:19:56,412
I think the very notion
that we could challenge them

436
00:19:56,543 --> 00:19:57,979
is near impossible as of now.

437
00:19:58,109 --> 00:19:59,937
- [Beezel] So you finally
realized it.

438
00:20:00,068 --> 00:20:01,939
- We should be thinking
how we can maintain

439
00:20:02,070 --> 00:20:03,898
an amicable relationship
with them,

440
00:20:04,028 --> 00:20:06,335
and if we could marry off
someone from the kingdom

441
00:20:06,466 --> 00:20:09,643
to their village, then it would
guarantee our safety here.

442
00:20:09,773 --> 00:20:10,818
- [Galgardo] No way.

443
00:20:10,948 --> 00:20:11,949
- What?

444
00:20:12,080 --> 00:20:13,647
- I won't hand over Yuri.

445
00:20:13,777 --> 00:20:15,083
Not to anyone ever.

446
00:20:15,214 --> 00:20:17,303
No matter what!

447
00:20:17,433 --> 00:20:19,218
- [Beezel] Please calm down.

448
00:20:20,436 --> 00:20:21,959
- [Michael] Did you gather
all the goods?

449
00:20:22,090 --> 00:20:23,352
- [Employee] Yes.

450
00:20:23,483 --> 00:20:24,875
- It'll leave a poor impression

451
00:20:25,006 --> 00:20:26,834
if we don't congratulate
them properly.

452
00:20:26,964 --> 00:20:29,402
We must make sure our
preparations are perfect.

453
00:20:29,532 --> 00:20:33,144
I want our relationship with
that village to continue.

454
00:20:34,058 --> 00:20:36,365
[bright gentle music]

455
00:20:37,845 --> 00:20:42,023
[cow mooing]
[wolf barks]

456
00:20:42,153 --> 00:20:43,590
- [Tia] Is something the matter?

457
00:20:43,720 --> 00:20:45,722
- [Hiraku] No, it's nothing.

458
00:20:45,853 --> 00:20:48,943
I just had a dream for
the first time in a while.

459
00:20:54,862 --> 00:20:59,083
[children laughing]

460
00:20:59,214 --> 00:21:01,825
- Could it be that you
have a hangover?

461
00:21:01,956 --> 00:21:04,219
- But you didn't drink
last night either.

462
00:21:04,350 --> 00:21:06,743
- You're right, I'm fine.

463
00:21:06,874 --> 00:21:09,180
- Oh, good.
- Hmm?

464
00:21:09,311 --> 00:21:11,400
- In that case, I wanna
talk about something

465
00:21:11,531 --> 00:21:14,403
that Granmaria and
the others brought up.

466
00:21:14,534 --> 00:21:16,536
- [Hiraku] People that
want to move here?

467
00:21:16,666 --> 00:21:17,972
- Yes.

468
00:21:18,102 --> 00:21:19,843
They were all living in
a different forest,

469
00:21:19,974 --> 00:21:23,064
but now they're looking for
somewhere new to live.

470
00:21:23,194 --> 00:21:25,719
- Dryme has some people that
were driven out of their homes

471
00:21:25,849 --> 00:21:27,460
because of a war.

472
00:21:27,590 --> 00:21:29,592
- My father also mentioned
that there are some refugees

473
00:21:29,723 --> 00:21:31,855
that need a place to stay
because of a war.

474
00:21:31,986 --> 00:21:33,204
- How many are there?

475
00:21:33,335 --> 00:21:34,945
- It's not exact, but...
- Um, let's see.

476
00:21:35,076 --> 00:21:36,207
- A rough estimate.

477
00:21:36,338 --> 00:21:37,992
- We broke the three digit mark.

478
00:21:38,122 --> 00:21:40,168
I think we need another
village like this

479
00:21:40,299 --> 00:21:41,865
if we're going to take
that many people

480
00:21:41,996 --> 00:21:43,606
- Well, then let's do it.

481
00:21:43,737 --> 00:21:44,694
- Huh?

482
00:21:44,825 --> 00:21:46,043
- Let's build a new village

483
00:21:46,174 --> 00:21:48,002
for all the people that
want to move here.

484
00:21:48,132 --> 00:21:49,612
- Ah, that sounds great.

485
00:21:49,743 --> 00:21:51,962
- If we do that, then lots of
people can move here.

486
00:21:52,093 --> 00:21:53,964
- It'll be the
Great Tree Village Two.

487
00:21:54,095 --> 00:21:55,444
- Wait a minute now.

488
00:21:55,575 --> 00:21:57,228
Won't that be a ton of
work for everyone?

489
00:21:57,359 --> 00:21:58,708
We need to gather supplies.

490
00:21:58,839 --> 00:22:01,581
- [All] We'll do our best.

491
00:22:01,711 --> 00:22:04,279
- After all, this village saved
each and every one of us.

492
00:22:04,410 --> 00:22:06,150
- If someone is needing our help

493
00:22:06,281 --> 00:22:08,239
we can't just leave them alone.

494
00:22:08,370 --> 00:22:10,154
- [Flowrem] Still, we'll need
to plan everything out

495
00:22:10,285 --> 00:22:11,504
very carefully for this.

496
00:22:11,634 --> 00:22:13,984
- [Lea] Where should
we build it?

497
00:22:14,115 --> 00:22:16,160
- [Hiraku] All right,
let's meet on it now.

498
00:22:16,291 --> 00:22:17,988
I'm counting on
your help everyone.

499
00:22:18,119 --> 00:22:20,034
- [All] Yeah.

500
00:22:22,645 --> 00:22:25,953
["Feel the winds" by
Yui Hizuki plays]

